      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2014. Published by Elsevier B.V.",
        "AbstractText": [
          {
            "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
            "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
            "content": "Serous tumors can occur on the surface of the ovaries and-rarely-as primary tumors on the peritoneal surface. However, the origin of extraovarian serous tumors is unknown. An unusual case of a serous tumor is presented here."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
            "Label": "CASE REPORT",
            "content": "A 34-year-old nulligravid woman presented for evaluation of her primary infertility, with acute abdominal pain. At laparoscopy, a paratubal cyst, independent of the ovaries, was found to be associated with bilateral hydrosalpinges. The final pathology diagnosis was of a benign paratubal serous cystadenoma."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
            "Label": "CONCLUSION",
            "content": "We present an unusual case of a paratubal serous cystadenoma with bilateral hydrosalpinges in an infertile woman, which was resected laparoscopically.."
          }
        ]
      },
